course: dictionary
lesson: 10241
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word token is a good example. In a board game, a token is a small piece you move around the board. In a shop, a token can be a voucher you swap for goods.
explain: Look at the words around the token. «A peppercorn rent now means a tiny token payment.» The word tiny tells you the payment is small. The word payment tells you money is involved, so here token means a small payment that stands for something, not the full amount.
explain: Token can also be an adjective. A token effort is small and done only for show, so the person is not really trying hard. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A token can be a round piece of metal or plastic used instead of a coin, for example in games or machines.
fact: A token can be a card or voucher that you exchange for goods, such as a book token.
fact: A token of something is a sign or symbol of a feeling, such as a token of thanks.
fact: As an adjective, «token» means small and done only for show, as in a token effort.
fact: In computers, a token is a piece of text or a code that a program reads, or that proves who you are.
exercise: «A peppercorn rent now means a tiny token payment.» What does token mean here? | A sport played with a ball | A game piece you move on a board | A huge payment made with lots of coins | *A small payment that stands for something, not the full amount
exercise: In a board game, what is a token? | A story told by a grandparent | A large map of the country | A loud whistle | *A small piece you move around the board
exercise: Which sentence uses token to mean small and done only for show? | She ran the fastest race of the day | The token was printed on shiny card | The shop gave her a book token worth ten pounds | *He made a token effort to tidy up, doing one shelf and then stopping
test: Ella gives her friend a card, «a token of thanks». What is a token of thanks? | *A sign that shows she is grateful | A coin from another country | A computer code | A rude reply
test: A book token is most like which of these? | A library rule | A page torn from a book | A bookshelf | *A voucher you can swap for a book
exam: In a computer program, what is a token? | A keyboard key that you press twice | A tiny insect that lives in the sea | A kind of computer screen | *A piece of text or code that a program reads, or that proves who you are
